---
title: Roast Duckling Montmorency
servings: 4
prepTime: 15 min
cookTime: 2.5 hours
description: Roast Duckling Montmorency (Canard à la Montmorency) is a classic French dish featuring roast duckling paired with a rich, sweet-and-savory sauce made with tart Montmorency cherries.
source: Meal-Master Library
tags: Alcohol
---

= Roast Duck =
Preheat the oven to 350°F.

Prick the skin of the @duck{5%lb} all over with a fork.
Place the duck in a roasting pan.
Surround the bird with @onion{1}(quartered), @carrots{2}(coarsely chopped),
and @celery{2%stalks}(coarsely chopped). Add @water{3%cups}.

> The vegetables will be discarded after roasting, so the cut preparation is not critical.

Roast, uncovered, in the oven for 25 minutes per pound, or about ~{2.5%hrs},
until cooked through.

= Cherry Sauce =
While the duck is roasting, bring 2 1/2 cups of @./Sauces/Classic Espagnole Sauce{1} to a boil
and reduce to 1 1/4 cups.

> Espagnole sauce (or brown sauce) is one of the five classic French mother sauces of classical cuisine,
> built on a rich brown roux, a flavorful mirepoix, tomato purée, and a deep brown veal or beef stock. 
> The sauce is deeply savory, rich with umami, layered with roasted notes, and bold in taste.

Drain @cherries{14%oz}(canned), reserving 1/2 cup of cherry juice.
Combine the reduced Espagnole sauce, reserved cherry juice,
@Cream Sherry{1/2%cup}, @orange rind{2%tsp}(grated), and @orange juice{1/4%cup}.

Remove the duck from the pan and keep warm.
Discard the vegetables from the pan juices and drain off all fat.

Stir 1 cup of the pan juices into the Espagnole mixture.
Bring the sauce to a boil, and reduce to 1 1/4 cups while stirring constantly.

Add @powdered sugar{3%tbsp}, @cinnamon{pinch}, and @cream cheese{8%oz}(cubed),
stir until smooth.
Stir in the drained cherries.

Carve the duck and serve with the cherry sauce.
